capability crypto/shake  SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 read to any length, and cSHAKE under a name and a customization
  heroes  crypto.shake128, crypto.shake256, crypto.Shake, crypto.ShakeState, crypto.start_shake, crypto.start_cshake, crypto.update_shake, crypto.digest_shake
  go      sha3.SumSHAKE128, sha3.SumSHAKE256, sha3.SHAKE, sha3.NewSHAKE128, sha3.NewSHAKE256, sha3.NewCSHAKE128, sha3.NewCSHAKE256, sha3.SHAKE.BlockSize, sha3.SHAKE.Read, sha3.SHAKE.Reset, sha3.SHAKE.Write
  rust    -
  python  hashlib.shake_128, hashlib.shake_256
  note    each read answers the output from its first byte, as Python's `digest(length)` does, where Go's `Read` goes on from the last read; a longer read begins with a shorter one, so Go's two reads are one read of their sum. A negative length is `invalid`, as Python refuses it. cSHAKE answered SP 800-185's samples 1 and 4 and a named case as Go did on 2026-11-17; with an empty name and customization it is SHAKE, as both standard and Go say. Python offers no cSHAKE

