capability crypto/scrypt  a key derived from a password by scrypt
  heroes  crypto.scrypt, crypto.MAX_MEMORY
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  hashlib.scrypt
  note    RFC 7914's vectors 1 to 3 and its Salsa20/8 vector answered as Python did on 2026-11-17 (vectors 2 and 3, 1 MiB × 16 and 16 MiB: the test run of the whole package grew from 9.65 s to 14.33 s of wall when they and their checks came in); vector 4 asks 1 GiB and runs nowhere here. Python's `maxmem` (32 MiB by default, OpenSSL's) is the constant `MAX_MEMORY`, 2 GiB, over 128 × r × (n + p) bytes, so vector 4 is allowed and a call cannot ask without bound; every refusal of Python's (n no power of two, n not below 2^(16r), r × p from 2^30, a length of 0) is one here. Go's is `golang.org/x/crypto/scrypt`, outside its standard library

